Method Code:
208 :   private Node tryFoldSimpleFunctionCall(Node n) {
209 :     Preconditions.checkState(n.isCall());
210 :     Node callTarget = n.getFirstChild();
211 :     if (callTarget != null && callTarget.isName() &&
212 :           callTarget.getString().equals("String")) {
213 :       // Fold String(a) to '' + (a) on immutable literals,
214 :       // which allows further optimizations
215 :       //
216 :       // We can't do this in the general case, because String(a) has
217 :       // slightly different semantics than '' + (a). See
218 :       // http://code.google.com/p/closure-compiler/issues/detail?id=759
219 :       Node value = callTarget.getNext();
220 :       if (value != null) {
221 :         Node addition = IR.add(
222 :             IR.string("").srcref(callTarget),
223 :             value.detachFromParent());
224 :         n.getParent().replaceChild(n, addition);
225 :         reportCodeChange();
226 :         return addition;
227 :       }
228 :     }
229 :     return n;
230 :   }
Hypothesis: The method only checks whether a first argument exists (value != null) and ignores whether there are additional arguments. For calls with 2+ arguments, replacing the whole call with '' + firstArg changes semantics by removing side effects of later arguments such as bar(). It should only fold when the call has exactly one argument.

